# Intended behaviour (pj_app ARCHITECTURE "One layout over several datasets"): a layout that names no dataset, whose
# curves come from two loaded files with no topic in common (data/sine only in data.csv, run/value only in run.csv),
# restores both curves unasked: only a topic several files carry is shared, so nothing is chosen or pinned. The
# browser's File > Save Layout writes such a layout for any session plotting two files.
# app: -d tests/wasm/fixtures/signals/data.csv -d scripts/qa/regressions/fixtures/compare_runs/run1/run.csv -l scripts/qa/regressions/fixtures/compare_runs/mixed_topics.pj4.xml
# needs: plugins
until get_status {} "name":"run.csv"
until ui_plot {"title":"Mixed"} "run/value"
expect "data/sine"
# No Layout warning: a dataset chosen for it would read "Warning | Layout | Layout '…' fits 2 loaded datasets". Filtered
# first, since the list shows only the rows in its viewport.
ui_click {"name":"buttonNotifications","wait_ms":500}
ui_click {"name":"searchBox","wait_ms":200}
ui_type {"text":"Layout","wait_ms":500}
ui_tree {}
expect QLineEdit "Layout"
expect | Info | Layout | Loaded layout
absent | Warning | Layout |
ui_key {"keys":"Escape"}
